Package: gliph2rs
Title: Fast GLIPH2 Convergence Groups for TCR Repertoires
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Mayank", "Gandhi", email = "gandhi.may@northeastern.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Mayank Gandhi [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Mayank Gandhi <gandhi.may@northeastern.edu>
Description: Groups T-cell receptor CDR3 beta sequences that are predicted to
    share antigen specificity, following the GLIPH2 method of Huang et al.
    (2020) <doi:10.1038/s41587-020-0505-4>. Group membership matches
    'turboGliph' exactly, while the computation runs in parallel Rust and
    scales to pooled cohorts of 100 million sequences. Also tests groups for
    association with a donor condition, such as cytomegalovirus serostatus.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
